<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Two Weapon Style</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Thief (guild level 19, up to 70%), Barbarian (guild level 10), Assassin (guild level 10)
</p><p>When you wield one weapon and hold another (see <a cmd='#'>Help Wield</a>), you fight
with both, striking with each in turn. Two weapon style is how well you
manage it.
</p><p>Fighting with two weapons is clumsy at first: your attacks with the
wielded weapon get a penalty of 25, and those with the held one a penalty
of 50. Every 4% of two weapon style takes a point off both, so at 100%
the wielded weapon strikes as well as it would alone, and the held one
still has a penalty of 25. Practising it needs dexterity 30.
</p><p>See also:
</p>
<pre> &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Wield</a>
</pre>




</div>